RHE 1993 XI 2 Garcia.Zuniga.pdf%3bjsessionid=39822A8B5CD2F4B016BABAA88D83B119", "url": "https://e-archivo.uc3m.es/bitstream/handle/10016/1911/RHE-1993-XI-2-Garcia.Zuniga.pdf%3bjsessionid=39822A8B5CD2F4B016BABAA88D83B119?sequence=1"}, {"title": "e-archivo.uc3m.es", "url": "https://e-archivo.uc3m.es/rest/api/core/item/e64e2105-3f8c-423c-b301-1abaf5595228/export/refworks"}, {"title": "The Enlightenment and Bourbon Reforms", "url": "https://lugares.inah.gob.mx/en/pagina-de-elemento/2380"}, {"title": "Publication: Haciendas forales y reformas borbónicas. Navarra, 1700-1808", "url": "https://e-archivo.uc3m.es/entities/publication/e64e2105-3f8c-423c-b301-1abaf5595228/full"}, {"title": "revistas.usal.es", "url": "https://revistas.usal.es/dos/index.php/1576-7914/article/download/3819/3834/12084"}, {"title": "Journal: | Investigación económica |", "url": "https://biblat.unam.mx/en/revista/investigacion-economica/articulo/los-limites-institucionales-del-crecimiento-economico-avances-y-retrocesos-de-la-politica-borbonica-en-el-siglo-xviii-novohispano"}, {"title": "IDEAS home Printed from https://ideas.repec.org/a/cup/reveco/v11y1993i02p307-334_00.html", "url": "https://ideas.repec.org/a/cup/reveco/v11y1993i02p307-334_00.html"}, {"title": "הרפורמות הבורבוניות", "url": "https://www.hamichlol.org.il/%D7%94%D7%A8%D7%A4%D7%95%D7%A8%D7%9E%D7%95%D7%AA_%D7%94%D7%91%D7%95%D7%A8%D7%91%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%95%D7%AA"}]}, "The search didn't turn up anything specific to infanzones. The results cover Bourbon fiscal policy in the Basque provinces and Navarre, which is related but not the same thing.\n\n- **Navarre and the Basque lands:** A 1993 article by Mario García-Zuñiga examines how the Bourbons reformed the finances of territories that had not been paying their share. In the 18th century the Bourbons undertook a series of reforms to integrate those territories which did not contribute. The author notes that the statutory finances of these territories were modified, although they continued to enjoy tax exemption. The article is the best lead here, but it is about provincial privileges, not the infanzón status.\n- **Álava and salt:** Rosario Porres Marijuán's study covers a dispute between the province of Álava and the Crown over salt taxes in the early Bourbon period. It also notes that the key date of this reform phase was 1740, when direct administration of revenue by the Crown was implanted.\n- **Broader Bourbon reforms:** A Salamanca review of a 2023 volume on the early Bourbons discusses the tension between privilege (tax exemption) and, on the other hand, the notion of the common good. That is the general theme you are after, though the snippet doesn't mention infanzones.\n\nNothing I found addresses how infanzón hidalgo exemptions specifically were treated under the Enlightenment reforms. For that, search Spanish-language sources on the \"exención fiscal de los infanzones\" or on the Bourbon *catastro* (the 1749 Ensenada cadastre) and the abolition of tax privileges."], "durationSeconds": 6.548561625000002, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01FCCMxPgoZPCyv8JKSZQ1MT", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
